  "body": "AGENTS.md Issue Law (user, 2026-11-08):\n\n- `gh pr create` gains `--draft`: every PR opens as a draft and stays one while work, gating and review fixes land on it.\n- New rule 'Every PR opens as a draft'. A PR is flagged ready (`gh pr ready`) only when the user says so, or when its gate is green on the final head and its independent review is clean.\n- Once a PR is ready, its branch takes no more pushes. A late fix or a merge of main turns it back into a draft first (`gh pr ready --undo`) with a PR comment, then it's re-gated and flagged ready again.\n- Only a ready PR merges.\n\nDocs-only, so there are no tests. Left as a draft for the user's OK, per the rule itself.\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
